								"value": "Bearer {{auth_token}}",
								"type": "text"
							},
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"content\": \"Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy. It occurs in the chloroplasts of plant cells, primarily in the leaves. The process involves two main stages: the light-dependent reactions and the light-independent reactions (Calvin cycle). During the light-dependent reactions, water molecules are split to produce oxygen and ATP. The Calvin cycle uses CO2 and ATP to produce glucose. Chlorophyll, the green pigment in plants, plays a crucial role in capturing light energy. The overall equation for photosynthesis is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + light energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2.\",\n  \"title\": \"Photosynthesis (Enhanced Mode)\",\n  \"config\": {\n    \"num_cards\": 8,\n    \"include_hints\": true,\n    \"card_style\": \"mixed\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"medium\",\n    \"mode\": \"enhanced\"\n  }\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/flashcards/generate/text",
							"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
							"path": ["api", "flashcards", "generate", "text"]
						},
						"description": "Generate flashcards using ENHANCED mode (RAG-based).\\n\\n**Enhanced Mode Features:**\\n- Uses RAG pipeline with concept extraction\\n- Applies Bloom's taxonomy levels\\n- Higher quality cards with better context\\n- Costs 2 credits (vs 1 for standard)\\n\\n**Enhanced Card Fields:**\\n- concept_name: The concept this card tests\\n- bloom_level: remember, understand, apply, analyze\\n- difficulty_score: 0.0 to 1.0\\n- source_chunk_id: RAG chunk reference\\n\\n**Generation Stats Include:**\\n- concepts_extracted: Number of concepts found\\n- chunks_processed: Number of document chunks\\n- timing breakdown"
